window.docContents[136].resolve({"/Foundations/#PDEAtlas--Foundations--Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus--Boundary-Calculus-and-C___-Boundary-Geometry--Scope-of-the-boundary-calculus":{"contents":"The finite compatible chart family assembles into a unique frontier-supported\nmeasure  with the same null sets as intrinsic Hausdorff\nsurface measure. Density-root rescaling identifies the finite-exponent Lᵖ\nspaces of the two measures isometrically, and for finite  the\nintrinsic trace has a norm-preserving atlas-coordinate form.\n\nMathlib supplies the same-dimensional Jacobian change of variables used for\nchart transitions, Hausdorff-measure transport under isometries, and Lipschitz\nnull-set transport. The nonlinear codimension-one area formula, which\nidentifies  with Hausdorff surface measure, is proved in\nthe trace development.\n\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Foundations\u0009Coordinates and Boundary Calculus\u0009Boundary Calculus and C¹ Boundary Geometry","header":"3.3.2.16. Scope of the boundary calculus","id":"/Foundations/#PDEAtlas--Foundations--Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus--Boundary-Calculus-and-C___-Boundary-Geometry--Scope-of-the-boundary-calculus"},"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--External-library-boundary":{"contents":"The scalar theory uses Mathlib's BesselPotentialSpace, together with its\nFourier transform, Schwartz space, tempered distributions,  spaces, and\ncontinuous linear maps. Physlib's quantum-mechanical Sobolev submodule is\n-based and narrower than the distribution-valued real-order scale used\nhere.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Sobolev Spaces and Weak Derivatives\u0009Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Sobolev Coverage and Open Problems","header":"4.6.1.14. External-library boundary","id":"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--External-library-boundary"}});